"Gods bring some outlanders on purpose: Emeric swapped souls with one to flee his wife's grasp."
"Maradoc collects entertaining outlanders, and enjoys watching them."
"A soul swapped in by a god arrives torn; its new body is formed bald and naked at a power locus."
"A god may leave a tiny bit of himself in an outlander, shown as a divine spark."
"Maradoc's blessing occults an outlander's status from inspection, though not their looks."
"Nous gives outlanders a blessing that speeds their learning; the Academy only suspects it."
"Time runs differently between worlds: about two years on Nyil were thirty-three on Earth."
"An alcove in Maradoc's House of Many Gates opens onto Earth."
"An outlander's fate is not Nyil's, so fate magic binds them poorly."
"The world allows only one Ascender; when two outlanders both ascend, one of them must die."
"Viviane was brought to Nyil because her talent would be wasted in a world without magic."
